# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data — never commit. See README for how to obtain it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/sickle_data/
*.zip
*.npz
*.tif
*.pth
*.pth.tar

# Reference implementation is cloned, not vendored (see README)
/reference_impl/

# Scratch
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODE ONLY in git, for now.
#
# results/ and outputs/ are NOT tracked: this repository carries the code and
# the fixes, not the numbers. They are regenerated by running the project, and
# every script that writes them is committed, so nothing is lost.
#
# artifacts/ IS tracked: the subset manifests under artifacts/subsets/ are
# referenced by configs (data.subset) and are inputs to a run, not outputs.
#
# When the study is finished and the numbers are final, drop the two rules at
# the bottom of this file to start committing the evidence alongside the code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
# The project's own interpreter lives at .venv -- 5+ GB, never committed.
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVIDENCE is tracked; WEIGHTS and LOGS are not.
#
# A run manifest records a git commit hash and git_dirty. That is meaningless
# unless the manifest itself is in the tree, so the per-run JSON is committed:
#     manifest.json          what produced the run
#     config_resolved.json   the fully merged config
#     trainlog.json          per-epoch metrics
#     best.json              selected epoch
#     best_per_plot_iou.json per-plot IoU at that epoch
# plus the aggregated tables under results/ (*.json, *.csv).
#
# ~2-3 MB in total. The checkpoints (686 MB of *.pth.tar) and the raw stdout
# logs stay out.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY, so the directories
# are un-ignored first (`!/outputs/**/`) and then the file types.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/outputs/**
!/outputs/**/
!/outputs/**/*.json
/outputs/logs/**

/results/**
!/results/**/
!/results/**/*.json
!/results/**/*.csv

# A README inside outputs/ explains evidence kept there; keep it.
!/outputs/_interrupted_runs/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SICKLE LABELS stay out of git (2026-10-14). The dataset is shared only
# through its authors' access form and carries no licence, so no file that
# holds per-field labels, or values derived field by field from them, is
# committed. These rules come last so they override the evidence rules above.
# The files stay on disk, so every build and check still runs; after
# obtaining data access, regenerate them with:
#   scripts/regression_gate.py   -> results/regression_gate/crop_yield_*.json
#   scripts/yield_screen.py      -> results/triage/yield_per_field.csv
#   scripts/field_confusions.py  -> results/field_confusions/*.json
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/results/regression_gate/crop_yield_*.json
/results/triage/yield_per_field.csv
/results/field_confusions/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated manuscripts stay out until a venue is chosen (2026-10-14). The
# scripts that build them are committed; scripts/build_all.py regenerates all
# of them and docs/deliverable_hashes.json records what was built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/*.docx
/docs/*.pdf
/docs/*.xlsx
/docs/rse/

# Per-field confusion matrices for the sweep are label-derived (see above).
/results/sweep/field_confusions/
